{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Or it is made known to him.</b> It is written here regarding the individual and regarding the nasi who sins. Some explain: 'to him' is as if it said 'if it is made known.' But the Rav Bekhor Shor z\"l wrote: because the nasi and the individual bring an asham taluy, as it is written regarding the nasi: ועשה אחת מכל מצות ה' אלהיו — meaning that none knows but HaShem his Elohim, which is a case of uncertainty, and he brings an asham taluy; 'or it is made known to him' — then he brings a chatat. And so you expound it regarding the individual, for it is written there: ממצות ה'. And a proof is from Torat Kohanim, which expounds: ואשם — this teaches that he brings an asham taluy. But the congregation and the anointed kohen do not bring an asham taluy — the congregation, for it is written here: נפש אחת תחטא, which implies 'one' and not the congregation; the anointed kohen, for it is written regarding him: לאשמת העם — the anointed kohen is like the congregation. Therefore 'or it is made known' is not written regarding them."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:50.773429755Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}